<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-2795] Cache query cursor do not create value copy</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-2795</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;If entries returned from SQL query are modified, these changes are reflected in the cache.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test attached.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="12948919">IGNITE-2795</key>
            <summary>Cache query cursor do not create value copy</summary>
                <type id="1" iconUrl="https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/viewavatar?size=xsmall&amp;avatarId=21133&amp;avatarType=issuetype">Bug</type>
                                            <priority id="3" iconUrl="https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/priorities/major.svg">Major</priority>
                        <status id="6" iconUrl="https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/statuses/closed.png" description="The issue is considered finished, the resolution is correct. Issues which are not closed can be reopened.">Closed</status>
                    <statusCategory id="3" key="done" colorName="green"/>
                                    <resolution id="1">Fixed</resolution>
                                        <assignee username="-1">Unassigned</assignee>
                                    <reporter username="vkulichenko">Valentin Kulichenko</reporter>
                        <labels>
                    </labels>
                <created>Thu, 10 Mar 2016 21:44:18 +0000</created>
                <updated>Fri, 19 Aug 2016 10:33:58 +0000</updated>
                            <resolved>Fri, 19 Aug 2016 10:32:39 +0000</resolved>
                                    <version>1.5.0.final</version>
                                    <fixVersion>1.8</fixVersion>
                                    <component>cache</component>
                        <due></due>
                            <votes>0</votes>
                                    <watches>5</watches>
                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="15362831" author="ascherbakov" created="Tue, 5 Jul 2016 17:32:38 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;The issue is also reproducible with cache iterator.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15364014" author="ascherbakov" created="Wed, 6 Jul 2016 08:56:35 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Fixed for SQL queries.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I&apos;m not sure the fix should be used at all, because it&apos;ll add performance overhead without any obvious benefits.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;PR &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/854&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/854&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15366291" author="ascherbakov" created="Thu, 7 Jul 2016 15:43:22 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Made better fix for SQL queries.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15391430" author="sboikov" created="Mon, 25 Jul 2016 06:55:29 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Alexei, I reviewed your fix, I think better fix is handle copying during GridQueryNextPageResponse creation: it is more optimal - you never need copy if response is sent to remote node and you do not need reflection hack in GridH2ResultSetIterator. Also please merge latest master, there was minor conflict.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15422977" author="ascherbakov" created="Tue, 16 Aug 2016 16:23:18 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Sam, thanks for review.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Using GridQueryNextPageResponse won&apos;t help us to keep correct read semantics in case of local SQL query.&lt;br/&gt;
In that case GridQueryNextPageResponse  is not used at all.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;See CacheSqlQueryValueCopySelfTest.testLocalSqlQuery test for details.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15424230" author="sboikov" created="Wed, 17 Aug 2016 09:55:18 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Alexei,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We must not do copy of data which is sent to remote node. If GridQueryNextPageResponse is not used for local queries, then for local queries copying should be implemented in iterators created in IgniteH2Indexing.queryLocalSqlFields/queryLocalSql.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15424415" author="ascherbakov" created="Wed, 17 Aug 2016 12:26:40 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Sam,&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We already do no data copying before sending it to remote node. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Concerning copy handling in GridH2ResultSetIterator wrapper for local queries I see only the possibility to use marshaller for producing data copy&lt;br/&gt;
by serialize/deserialize process, which is less efficient than current approach requiring only deserialization.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Are you sure we must implement copy handling in such way ?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15424823" author="ascherbakov" created="Wed, 17 Aug 2016 16:12:15 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Made optimization to do copying only for local node data.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15424826" author="ascherbakov" created="Wed, 17 Aug 2016 16:13:00 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Waiting for TC.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15427978" author="sboikov" created="Fri, 19 Aug 2016 10:32:39 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Thanks Alexei, merged into master (commit #612eb3d).&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
